  "_note": "HydroControl fan curve for the HYDROC-16 G1. OURS, not vendor data: derived from measurements on this machine (fans engage near 55 C, PWM scale is 0-200 with the register holding Duty*2) and from the safety reasoning below. The vendor UserFanTables in hydroc-driver/ were NOT used -- they are for lower-power chassis (PL1 40-60 W against our measured 75 W default, PROJECT_ID 0x19 is past the end of that table) and copying them would not make them MIT. DELIBERATELY MORE AGGRESSIVE THAN STOCK: it ramps from 40 C where the firmware is silent to 55 C, and never commands less than 30%. If ENABLE_UNIVERSAL_FAN_CTRL turns out to be a one-way door like FAN_MODE_USER, the machine is then stuck loud rather than stuck hot. There is no temperature at which this curve turns the fans off.",
